#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-04.png", width: 500pt), 68.5pt, 253.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(295.08pt, 808.32pt, "4 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(36pt, 100.44pt, "to detect pipeline bursts and leaks, while [56] reviewed pressure-based techniques for leak monitoring in pipe ")
  #line-at(36pt, 132.96pt, "distribution systems. These studies focus on identifying the causes of anomalies in water supply networks, ")
  #line-at(36pt, 165.6pt, "which differs from our approach. In contrast, this study applies ARIMA models not for anomaly classification ")
  #line-at(36pt, 198.24pt, "but for pressure management by predicting P3 pressure based on head losses, optimizing the efficiency of ")
  #line-at(36pt, 230.76pt, "pressure control strategies. ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(83.16pt, 416.4pt, "Figure 1. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(132.24pt, 416.4pt, "Strategies for Pressure Reducing Valves (PRV) in Water Distribution Systems.")
  #line-at(61.56pt, 451.68pt, "There are different references that shows that the Box and Jenkins methodology (1976) is very suitable ")
  #line-at(36pt, 484.32pt, "for the analysis of the data service to predict the hydraulic performance of the network [28,29], in PRV with ")
  #line-at(36pt, 516.84pt, "open loop control strategy. This methodology proposed by Box and Jenkins is a statistical method used to ")
  #line-at(36pt, 549.48pt, "analyse and predict time series and is part of the general ARMA model. Their work, developed in the first five ")
  #line-at(36pt, 582.12pt, "years of the 1970s (Figure 2), has led to one of the methodologies most widely used in the predictive analysis ")
  #line-at(36pt, 614.64pt, "of numerical series [30]. The methodology has essentially three stages. Stage 1 consists of identifying the ")
  #line-at(36pt, 647.28pt, "model type and for this it is important to detect whether the data present patterns, trends, seasonal behaviour ")
  #line-at(36pt, 679.92pt, "or whether the series is stationary or not. Stage 2 consists of identifying the coefficients or parameters of the ")
  #line-at(36pt, 712.44pt, "model using maximum likelihood techniques and the last one consists of evaluating the accuracy of the model.  ")
  #line-at(61.56pt, 745.08pt, "The general model from which the Box and Jenkins methodology originates is composed of two models, ")
  #line-at(36pt, 777.72pt, "the AR (Autoregressive) model and the MA (Moving Average) model. The AR term represents the relationship ")
]

