  #line-at(61.56pt, 572.16pt, "The above general model presents variants depending on whether the time series considered in the ")
  #line-at(36pt, 597.48pt, "modelling is stationary or not, whether it presents seasonal behaviour and/or whether there are exogenous ")
  #line-at(36pt, 622.68pt, "factors that may influence the variable studied. According to the above, the existing variables are called ")
  #line-at(36pt, 648pt, "ARIMA, SARIMA, ARIMAX, ARMAX or SARIMAX. The I present in any of the models refers to the differenti-")
  #line-at(36pt, 673.32pt, "ation operation that may be carried out on the series. The seasonal component of the series is represented ")
  #line-at(36pt, 698.64pt, "by the letter S in the name of the model. If the series under study presents this behaviour, the model will be ")
  #line-at(36pt, 723.96pt, "assigned three coefficients (P, D, Q) representing the relationship between present and past observations ")
  #line-at(36pt, 749.16pt, "(P) and the relationship with the residual errors of paired values (Q). The (D) refers to the level of seasonal ")
]

// arXiv source page 6
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(295.08pt, 808.32pt, "6 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(36pt, 90.48pt, "differentiation made in the original series. If, in addition to the above, the models present an X at the end, it ")
  #line-at(36pt, 115.68pt, "means that they present exogenous variables [30]. ")
  #line-at(61.56pt, 141pt, "There are different uses for the general ARMA model and its ARIMA variant, with or without exogenous ")
  #line-at(36pt, 166.32pt, "variables. The studies performed with ARIMA models and their adaptations are diverse in different research ")
  #line-at(36pt, 191.64pt, "fields. Zhou et al. [31], Wong et al. [32] and Du et al. [33] used these models to forecast water consumption. ")
  #line-at(36pt, 216.96pt, "Liu et al. [34] studied acute haemorrhagic conjunctivitis and Makoni et al. [35] modelled tourism inflow in ")
  #line-at(36pt, 242.28pt, "Zimbabwe. Ampountolas [36] modelled and forecasted daily customer demand in a hotel using, among oth-")
  #line-at(36pt, 267.48pt, "ers, a SARIMAX model. Manigandan et al. [37] forecasted gas consumption in the United States. Yin et al. ")
  #line-at(36pt, 292.8pt, "[38] use an ARMAX model for output noise estimation in control engineering. Lim et al. [39] consider the ")
  #line-at(36pt, 318.12pt, "ARMAX model to estimate the travel demand of Japanese citizens to destinations such as New Zealand and ")
  #line-at(36pt, 343.44pt, "Taiwan. ")
  #line-at(61.56pt, 368.76pt, "The present study conducts an analysis of the data series from the Noja (Cantabria, Spain) potable ")
  #line-at(36pt, 393.96pt, "water network. With more than 80,000 real data points from the network, the best model is fitted and validated ")
  #line-at(36pt, 419.28pt, "using the Box and Jenkins methodology. The objective is to apply an innovative development of time series ")
  #line-at(36pt, 444.6pt, "analysis to open-loop critical point pressure management system to predict the pressure at the critical point ")
  #line-at(36pt, 469.92pt, "(P3). The pressure at the critical point (P3) depends on two exogenous variables: pressure at the outlet of ")
  #line-at(36pt, 495.24pt, "the pressure-reducing valve (P2), which is adjusted by the pressure reducing valve (PRV) and the flow rate ")
  #line-at(36pt, 520.56pt, "at the inlet of the area (Q), which depends of the total consumption demanded by the population. The model ")
  #line-at(36pt, 545.76pt, "will employ these two variables, P2 and Q to forecast the pressure at the critical point (P3). The model will ")
  #line-at(36pt, 571.08pt, "be applied with real data of a hydraulic network with seasonal demand where critical point pressure control ")
  #line-at(36pt, 596.4pt, "is essential to deliver water with the right level of service while minimizing leakages rates.")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(36pt, 621.72pt, "2. Materials and Methods ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(36pt, 647.04pt, "2.1. Description of Case Study area ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(57.24pt, 672.24pt, "This study's series have been analysed and validated with real data provided by the Noja water company. ")
  #line-at(36pt, 697.56pt, "Noja (Figure 3) is a coastal town in the Cantabria region, northern Spain. This town has a permanent popu-")
  #line-at(36pt, 722.88pt, "lation of approximately 2700 inhabitants, which increases by more than 3600 % during the summer, reaching ")
  #line-at(36pt, 748.2pt, "up to 100,000 people during the holiday period. Therefore, Noja has a very seasonal demand with great ")
  #line-at(36pt, 773.52pt, "variation between winter and holiday periods, such as Easter or summer. ")
]

