  #line-at(119.16pt, 374.88pt, "Figure 5. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(168.24pt, 374.88pt, "P3 and PRV location in Noja and the area supplied by the PRV. ")
  #line-at(57.24pt, 400.2pt, "The P3 target critical points values are selected by the water operator. The P3 values are chosen to ")
  #line-at(36pt, 425.52pt, "secure the right level of service in the area. During the central time of the day, when the demand is higher, ")
  #line-at(36pt, 450.84pt, "the P3 values are higher to secure optimal service to the customers. During the night period, when the con-")
  #line-at(36pt, 476.04pt, "sumption is lower and demand reduced, the P3 values are lower to minimize water lost by leakages. This ")
  #line-at(36pt, 501.36pt, "PRV is based on an open-loop Critical Point Control (CPC) method, where pressure modulation at P2 de-")
  #line-at(36pt, 526.68pt, "pends on flow variations to ensure pressure stabilisation at P3 (Figure 6). The flow data essential for this ")
  #line-at(36pt, 552pt, "control mechanism is derived from the pulse output of a water meter located downstream of the PRV. To ")
  #line-at(36pt, 577.32pt, "prevent interference with the valve's original pressure reduction pilot, the electronic controller is installed in ")
  #line-at(36pt, 602.52pt, "parallel and isolated. In addition, upstream and downstream pressures are recorded at 15 minutes intervals ")
  #line-at(36pt, 627.84pt, "with a sampling frequency of 10 seconds. The controller adjusts the valve outlet pressure according to the ")
  #line-at(36pt, 653.16pt, "prescribed pressure management protocol, maintaining an industry standard deadband of ±0.5 m. A data ")
  #line-at(36pt, 678.48pt, "logger positioned at the critical point records pressure data using the same logging interval and sampling ")
  #line-at(36pt, 703.8pt, "rate. ")
]

