#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(292.68pt, 808.32pt, "13 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(57.24pt, 90.48pt, "The aim of this study is to develop and evaluate an innovative system for pressure management at the ")
  #line-at(36pt, 115.68pt, "critical point P3 of a drinking water distribution network using the Box Jenkins methodology and the model ")
  #line-at(36pt, 141pt, "that best fits the characteristics of the time series, ARMA or ARMAX (considering P3 as an exogenous vari-")
  #line-at(36pt, 166.32pt, "able). The main objective of this system is to predict the pressure at P3 as a function of the pressure at the ")
  #line-at(36pt, 191.64pt, "outlet of valve P2 and the flow rate in the network. This predictive system allows to modulate P2 pressure at ")
  #line-at(36pt, 216.96pt, "the outlet of the valve and detect abnormal water consumption, for example, due to water losses. Additionally, ")
  #line-at(36pt, 242.28pt, "it aims to provide accurate and real-time information on the pressure at P3 to support network maintenance ")
  #line-at(36pt, 267.48pt, "operations, improve leak detection and location, and optimize water use in the distribution network. This ")
  #line-at(36pt, 292.8pt, "predictive tool can be a great ally for water companies that use open control systems, saving costs and ")
  #line-at(36pt, 318.12pt, "improving service for end users. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(36pt, 343.44pt, "2.3. Modelling ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(57.24pt, 368.76pt, "For the analysis of time series, the Box-Jenkins methodology develops statistical models which consider ")
  #line-at(36pt, 393.96pt, "the dependence between data, so that the observation at an instant is modeled as a function of previous ")
  #line-at(36pt, 419.28pt, "values. In this section, the methodology used to select the model that best fits the data series is developed ")
  #line-at(36pt, 444.6pt, "(Figure 8). The Eviews software application, specially designed to work with ARIMA models, has been used ")
  #line-at(36pt, 469.92pt, "for data analysis. ")
  #line-at(57.24pt, 495.24pt, "The different variants of ARIMA models are based on the linear dependence of the time series Suhermi ")
  #line-at(36pt, 520.56pt, "et al. [40], Sau et al. [41] as well as on the stationarity of the data used for the Durdu model [42]. Previous ")
  #line-at(36pt, 545.76pt, "studies applied in different field sciences, such as, as energy consumption, stock prices and other economic ")
  #line-at(36pt, 571.08pt, "indicators Sau et al. [41], Durdu [43], Visutsak et al. [44], have shown that ARIMA models can provide accu-")
  #line-at(36pt, 596.4pt, "rate results. In the presence of non-linear dependencies of the considered parameters, ARIMA models, by ")
  #line-at(36pt, 621.72pt, "themselves, do not perform adequately. In these cases, the use of artificial neural networks (ANNs) or support ")
  #line-at(36pt, 647.04pt, "vector machines (SVMs), among others, together with ARIMA models, may be more effective Suhermi et al. ")
  #line-at(36pt, 672.24pt, "[40], Aradhye et al. [45], Man-Chun et al. [46]. In view of the technical problem posed, the objective of the ")
  #line-at(36pt, 697.56pt, "present study is to demonstrate the effectiveness of ARIMA models in predicting future pressure values. ")
  #line-at(57.24pt, 722.88pt, "The data series available is from February 28, 2021 to August 20, 2022. Thus, the series was divided ")
  #line-at(36pt, 748.2pt, "into two series, the first from February 28, 2021, to March 31, 2022 (38,112 data), was used to generate the ")
  #line-at(36pt, 773.52pt, "model and the second with data from 2022, from April 2022 to August 20, 2022 (13,631 data, was used to ")
]

