#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(292.68pt, 808.32pt, "24 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(36pt, 90.48pt, "additional exogenous factors to maintain the model's accuracy. This underscores the necessity for future ")
  #line-at(36pt, 115.68pt, "research to investigate the model's performance across a range of water distribution systems and operational ")
  #line-at(36pt, 141pt, "scenarios, as well as the potential for hybrid approaches combining predictive analytics with real-time ")
  #line-at(36pt, 166.32pt, "feedback mechanisms. ")
  #line-at(57.24pt, 191.64pt, "Applying this methodology in other regions or countries presents additional challenges, particularly in ")
  #line-at(36pt, 216.96pt, "systems with different infrastructure characteristics or operational constraints. For example, networks in ")
  #line-at(36pt, 242.28pt, "regions with limited data availability or less advanced monitoring systems may struggle to achieve the data ")
  #line-at(36pt, 267.48pt, "quality required for model training and validation. In addition, variations in topography, climate and population ")
  #line-at(36pt, 292.8pt, "dynamics may require model adaptations to ensure accurate predictions and robust performance in different ")
  #line-at(36pt, 318.12pt, "contexts. These considerations highlight the need for further research to assess the generalisability and ")
  #line-at(36pt, 343.44pt, "scalability of the model in different scenarios. ")
  #line-at(57.24pt, 368.76pt, "Finally, it is important to highlight that the proposed ARMAX model significantly contributes to ")
  #line-at(36pt, 393.96pt, "sustainability in water distribution systems. By optimizing pressure management and improving leak ")
  #line-at(36pt, 419.28pt, "detection, it reduces water losses, conserving this critical resource and decreasing the energy demand ")
  #line-at(36pt, 444.6pt, "associated with water treatment and pumping. This aligns with global efforts to promote sustainable water ")
  #line-at(36pt, 469.92pt, "management practices, particularly in areas facing increasing water scarcity. ")
  #line-at(57.24pt, 495.24pt, "Additionally, these improvements have a direct positive impact on local communities. A more efficient ")
  #line-at(36pt, 520.56pt, "water distribution system ensures a reliable supply of clean water, even during periods of peak demand, such ")
  #line-at(36pt, 545.76pt, "as those observed in Noja during the summer season. This enhances the quality of life for residents and ")
  #line-at(36pt, 571.08pt, "reduces the risks associated with intermittent water supplies, such as health concerns or disruptions to daily ")
  #line-at(36pt, 596.4pt, "activities. Furthermore, by lowering operational costs through reduced water loss and maintenance needs, ")
  #line-at(36pt, 621.72pt, "the proposed approach can enable water utilities to allocate resources to other critical infrastructure ")
  #line-at(36pt, 647.04pt, "improvements, further supporting community well-being. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(36pt, 672.24pt, "3.3. Model application ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(57.24pt, 697.56pt, "It must be highlithed that the model can apply only in areas fed through one single point. For mulifeed ")
  #line-at(36pt, 722.88pt, "areas, with more than one entry of water, this model would require to be reevaluted and adapted. However, ")
  #line-at(36pt, 748.2pt, "the most common application in water distribution system are single fed areas. ")
]

