  #line-at(57.24pt, 393.96pt, "In this work, only the ARIMA model has been considered, as well as its variant ARMAX, the new trends ")
  #line-at(36pt, 419.28pt, "of implanting mixed models, between the model studied and artificial neural networks (ANNs), is a clear ")
  #line-at(36pt, 444.6pt, "option for study, although the results obtained with the use of the ARMAX model are so good. Future studies ")
  #line-at(36pt, 469.92pt, "could explore the integration of mixed models with artificial neural networks (ANNs), leveraging boundary ")
  #line-at(36pt, 495.24pt, "conditions to better understand their influence on pressure variations like those observed at P3. This ")
  #line-at(36pt, 520.56pt, "approach could improve anomaly classification and enhance predictive capabilities for pressure management ")
  #line-at(36pt, 545.76pt, "in complex water distribution systems. ")
  #line-at(57.24pt, 571.08pt, "Finally, it is important to highlight the limitations and future opportunities of this line of research. The main ")
  #line-at(36pt, 596.4pt, "limitation is the type and size of the network with control at a single PRV. It would be interesting to apply this ")
  #line-at(36pt, 621.72pt, "model to larger networks with several control points to examine the robustness of predictive models based ")
  #line-at(36pt, 647.04pt, "on the analysis of data series. While the study focuses on a single PRV in the Noja network, this limitation ")
  #line-at(36pt, 672.24pt, "highlights the challenges of scaling the approach to larger, more complex networks. Larger networks often ")
  #line-at(36pt, 697.56pt, "have multiple critical points, interacting PRVs, and varying hydraulic conditions, which may require more ")
  #line-at(36pt, 722.88pt, "sophisticated models or hybrid approaches combining real-time data with predictive analytics. Additionally, ")
  #line-at(36pt, 748.2pt, "the dependency on historical data for model training could pose challenges in networks with incomplete or ")
  #line-at(36pt, 773.52pt, "inconsistent datasets, limiting the robustness of predictions in such scenarios. Future research should explore ")
]

// arXiv source page 27
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(292.68pt, 808.32pt, "27 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(36pt, 90.48pt, "how the ARMAX model performs in multi-PRV systems or networks with higher levels of variability, potentially ")
  #line-at(36pt, 115.68pt, "integrating additional exogenous factors or advanced feedback systems to improve adaptability and ")
  #line-at(36pt, 141pt, "scalability. ")
  #line-at(57.24pt, 166.32pt, "This model is ready to be implemented in Noja's pressure control system. The advantages of applying ")
  #line-at(36pt, 191.64pt, "the ARMAX model in critical point pressure management are clear, including improved leak detection and ")
  #line-at(36pt, 216.96pt, "location, enhanced network maintenance operations, and optimized water use efficiency. The implementation ")
  #line-at(36pt, 242.28pt, "of the ARMAX model in the Noja water distribution network would have significant practical impacts. From an ")
  #line-at(36pt, 267.48pt, "economic perspective, the ARMAX model has the potential to reduce water loss and associated costs by ")
  #line-at(36pt, 292.8pt, "facilitating more efficient and precise leak detection. From an environmental perspective, the model fosters ")
  #line-at(36pt, 318.12pt, "sustainable water management by optimising pressure levels and reducing unnecessary water wastage, ")
  #line-at(36pt, 343.44pt, "thereby contributing to the conservation of this vital resource. Operationally, the enhanced predictive ")
  #line-at(36pt, 368.76pt, "capabilities would support more efficient network maintenance, improving overall reliability and service quality ")
  #line-at(36pt, 393.96pt, "for end users. The model's potential to address key challenges in water distribution is evident in these ")
  #line-at(36pt, 419.28pt, "impacts, and it provides a scalable and sustainable solution for similar systems worldwide. By accurately ")
  #line-at(36pt, 444.6pt, "predicting pressure levels at critical points, operators can proactively address issues such as leaks, abnormal ")
  #line-at(36pt, 469.92pt, "consumption, and network anomalies. The ARMAX model provides valuable insights for water distribution ")
  #line-at(36pt, 495.24pt, "network operators, enabling them to detect pressure variations early and take preventive measures to ")
  #line-at(36pt, 520.56pt, "mitigate potential problems. Furthermore, by optimizing pressure levels throughout the network, operators ")
  #line-at(36pt, 545.76pt, "can reduce the risk of infrastructure damage, improve operational efficiency, and minimize system downtime. ")
  #line-at(36pt, 571.08pt, "By leveraging advanced technologies and data-driven solutions, water utilities can enhance their capacity to ")
  #line-at(36pt, 596.4pt, "ensure a reliable water supply, minimize water loss, and promote the sustainability of water resources for ")
  #line-at(36pt, 621.72pt, "future generations. This research will enhance the reliability of predictions, enabling management company ")
  #line-at(36pt, 647.04pt, "planners to make more robust decisions.")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(36pt, 682.2pt, "Acknowledgments: ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(140.04pt, 682.2pt, "The authors would like to thank GS Inima water utility for their contribution, availability, ")
  #line-at(36pt, 714.84pt, "criticism, and support to materialize this paper. ")
]

